- The James Webb Space Telescope helps scientists observe distant galaxies and study the early universe.
- Black holes help scientists understand gravity and the nature of space and time.

Explain the importance of studying space:

- It helps us understand how the universe began and evolved.
- It helps us discover new objects and phenomena.
- It improves our knowledge of physics and astronomy.
- It inspires future scientific research.

